# Half-Life HD rocket launcher. Measured by vrcardgen off valve_hd, finished
# by hand.
#
# ONE CARD, THREE GAME DIRECTORIES. valve_hd, gearbox_hd and bshift_hd all
# ship this same rig: 50 bones, 9 sequences, hash 0x1e3e8964, and the rocket
# seats at the same place in all three to three decimals. The three FILES are
# not identical - 197352, 228080 and 122120 bytes, bshift_hd being the small
# one because it keeps its textures outside the model - but binding is by
# fingerprint, not by bytes, so one card covers them and declines everything
# else. Retail SD is a different rig and still has no card: valve is 32 bones
# / 10 seqs / 0x862bb646, and gearbox and bshift are both 31 / 8 / 0x27652336.
# (cards/valve/v_rpg.card is 54 bones / 0x58602f2c - the VR tree's own model,
# not a retail one. It binds to none of these.)
#
# Part J: "Slide a rocket into the tube until it latches. Shoulder it. The
# laser follows the muzzle, so the rocket is steered by hand."
#
# ONE ROUND AND NO ACTION, the same verdict as the SD sibling. There is
# nothing on this launcher for a hand to work: no bolt, no magazine, no
# cover, no hammer. The rocket IS the loading gesture, and `single_shot` is
# built for exactly that - vr_gun.cpp:132 says so in as many words ("a weapon
# that does not need it - the RPG - simply leaves it undeclared and loads at
# the port"), and vr_feed.cpp:641's single-shot rule is literally "a rocket
# slid into the tube ... if the chamber is empty, what the hand is carrying
# goes in it". No `needs_cock` either: VRFeed_NeedsCocking already answers no
# for a SINGLE weapon, because a launcher has no striker to set, and one that
# insisted on being cocked would fire exactly once and then be inert.
#
#
# WHAT THE MODEL HAS. Three bones in the weapon subtree and no more, out of
# 872 vertices:
#
#   Rlauncher    463 verts, 53.1%, root-parented  - the body
#   Rocket        62 verts,  7.1%, child of body  - the rocket itself
#   Cylinder01    37 verts,  4.2%, child of body  - housing on the tube side
#
# The other 47 bones are the arm, hand and finger rig. The body's geometry
# gives the tube: the bore axis is the line x=-1.305 z=0.187, the muzzle is a
# ring of twelve vertices at radius 2.63-2.74 about that axis at y=-14.76,
# and the rear of the tube is at y=+9.46 - 24.22 units of tube, with the grip
# hanging to z=-8.05 under the middle of it. FORWARD IS -Y, which is what the
# rocket standing proud of the muzzle proves and what vrcardgen's fallback
# frame already assumes.
#
# THERE ARE NO ATTACHMENTS ON THIS MODEL - numattachments is 0 - so the
# muzzle that Part J's laser is meant to follow cannot be read off an
# attachment. It can be read off the geometry, and it is: (-1.305, -14.76,
# 0.187), pointing down -Y. The card format has no muzzle keyword, so that
# measurement is recorded in this comment and nowhere else.
#
#
# TRAP 1: `travel 60.90` IS NOT A MECHANISM. vrcardgen reports the Rocket
# bone travelling 60.90 units, and it does - but not into anything. That is
# the full span of its Z channel across all nine sequences, from +0.269
# part-way through `reload` to -60.628 part-way through `holster2`. The four
# EMPTY-launcher sequences - fire, idle2, draw2, holster2 - park the rocket
# at about (-1.305, +13.2, -58.1), 58.3 units below the seat, which is how
# the artists hid it on a launcher with nothing in the tube; the four LOADED
# ones - idle, fidget, draw1, holster1 - all hold it seated. 60.90 is the
# distance between a hiding place and a seat. The SD card met the same
# artefact and called it ten thousand units: same lie, different clothes.
#
# THE REAL INSERTION, posed off `reload` frame by frame: the hand brings the
# rocket in from (14.598, 7.663, -17.013) on frame 0, swings and aligns it in
# front of the muzzle through frame 33, then pushes it home over frames 33-38
# - 5.997 units along the bore. The rocket's tail finishes at y=-10.043,
# which is 4.72 units inside the muzzle ring, and its nose stands 8.69 units
# proud of it: THIS LAUNCHER IS MUZZLE-LOADED, like the RPG-7 it is drawn
# from. The rocket is 13.41 units long and its widest point is radius 1.86,
# against a bore of about 2.6.
#
# None of those is a joint travel, because the rocket is not a joint.
# vrcardgen classifies it as "arrives from outside - an object, not a joint",
# and the feed path owns it: the renderer draws it from chamber state, which
# is what makes the model's park-it-offscreen trick unnecessary.
#
# TRAP 2: `Cylinder01 hinge travel 6.23` IS A GIMBAL ALIAS, and the drafted
# card offers it as joint 0. Posing it says otherwise. Its euler channels
# flip frame to frame between (-1.571, -3.142, -1.571) and (+1.571, -6.283,
# +1.571), and those two eulers are the SAME ORIENTATION - both resolve to
# the matrix x=(0,1,0) y=(0,0,1) z=(1,0,0). The 6.225 radians is the encoder
# crossing a gimbal, not the part turning. Measured as an orientation rather
# than as a channel, the part tilts 0.3229 rad - 18.50 degrees - at frame 25
# of `fidget`, and EXACTLY ZERO in all eight other sequences; its vertices
# sweep 0.45 units further there than their static extent, and 0.00 anywhere
# else.
#
# So it stays undeclared, for three reasons. Taking joint 0 would hand the
# single_shot preset's sear and its hammer_cock detent to a sight housing.
# Declaring it at any index would take it off the fidget animation that is
# the only thing which ever moves it, freezing it. And eighteen degrees once
# per idle is not something a hand has any reason to reach for.

weapon v_rpg
match  bones 50  seqs 9  hash 0x1e3e8964

# The bone every position in this card is measured in - the controls, the
# grab points, the chamber, the ejection port. Nothing recorded it until
# the engine had to place a control in the world to ask whether a thumb is
# near it; the simulator never needed one, because it never works in world
# space. Taken from the generator, which has always called this bone the
# WEAPON BODY and is what measured these numbers in the first place.
body   "Rlauncher"

type   single_shot  rpm 150
# The rate is deliberately loose. On a weapon like this the MECHANISM is the
# limiter - you cannot shoot faster than you can get the next rocket out of
# the pouch and into the muzzle - so a low rpm only adds a second, invisible
# timer that refuses to fire when the player has done everything right. 150
# rpm is a 400 ms floor, there to keep two shots out of one millisecond and
# nothing more. Half-Life's own 1.5 s between shots was the length of an
# animation, and the animation is no longer in charge.
#
# NO JOINT LINES. `single_shot` declares joint 0 with a hammer_cock detent
# and a sear, and on this weapon that joint stays bone-less and inert on
# purpose: nothing engages a sear without `needs_cock`, and with no eject
# detent action_open is never set, so the launcher fires from rest the way it
# should. That is the preset used as written, not worked around.

# WHERE THE ROCKET SITS when the chamber is live: the Rocket bone's own rest
# origin in the weapon's frame, which is also where `reload` leaves it on
# frame 38 and where idle, fidget, draw1 and holster1 all hold it. Identical
# in valve_hd, gearbox_hd and bshift_hd. Part E has the renderer draw the
# chambered round's model at this position, and that is what replaces the
# model's park-it-offscreen trick for an empty tube.
chamber at -1.305 -16.423 0.187

# NO `eject`. "NOTHING IS LEFT BEHIND by a bolt or a rocket" - vr_feed.cpp
# empties the chamber rather than marking it spent on a SINGLE weapon, so
# there is no case to throw and no port to throw it through. There is none in
# the mesh either.
#
# NO `strike`. Part J gives every firearm a butt-stroke, and the parser hands
# the pistol-whip default to any card that declares none, which is what this
# one does. Twenty-four units of steel tube deserves better than the default,
# but a strike's two speeds are not measurable off a model and nobody has
# chosen them, so they stay at the default rather than being invented here.
